Faster file reading at startup, and a desktop that keeps running.

Every read and seek is a filing system call on RISC OS. Loading the sprite
tables jumps back and forth by a few bytes, and each jump used to throw
away the 512-byte buffer and seek again. On a desktop PC that was about
32,500 seeks and 11,000 reads at startup.
- RandomAccessFile: 32 KB buffer; SeekTo stays inside the buffer when it
  can, and doesn't seek when the file is already there; ReadBlock uses the
  buffered bytes first. Results are identical (checked over 800,000 random
  operations against the original code). On the PC the startup counts drop
  to about 1,400 seeks and 6,200 reads.
- The MD5 check of the base set files reads 32 KB at a time instead of 1 KB.
- Each buffer refill calls RiscOsKeepDesktopAlive() (patch 09), so the
  desktop is polled while graphics and sounds load.

For OpenTTD 14.1. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-openttd.

